Step 6 – Create GitHub Actions workflow
Create the folders:
mkdir .github
mkdir .github\workflows
notepad .github\workflows\ci-dockerhub.yml


Paste this complete workflow:

name: Python CI Docker Pipeline

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Python
        uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: '3.11'

      - name: Install pytest
        run: pip install pytest

      - name: Run tests
        run: python -m pytest -q

      - name: Login to Docker Hub
        uses: docker/login-action@v3
        with:
          username: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}
          password: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_TOKEN }}

      - name: Build and Push Docker Image
        uses: docker/build-push-action@v6
        with:
          context: .
          push: true
          tags: azcruze/python-ci-docker-lab:latest



Save and close Notepad.
Step 7 – Configure Docker Hub credentials
1. Open Docker Hub.
2. Create a public repository named python-ci-docker-lab.
3. Generate a Docker Hub access token.
4. Open your GitHub repository → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions.
5. Add these repository secrets:
Secret name	Value
DOCKERHUB_USERNAME	azcruze
DOCKERHUB_TOKEN	Your Docker Hub access token

Never put your access token directly in the workflow file.
